      en: "Gan HaShlosha National Park (also known as Sachne) is located in the Beit She'an Valley in northern Israel, near the green border with Jordan. The park is famous for its natural springs that maintain a pleasant water temperature of 28°C year-round. The pool is a popular swimming spot. The park includes an archaeological park with ruins of an ancient city. It has picnic areas, lawns, and shaded spots. The park was named after three early Jewish settlers killed in 1937 at Kibbutz Beit Alfa. The springs are rich in minerals and valued for their healing properties.",
