      en: "Meymadion (also known as Mekorot Water Park) is located near Netanya, Israel. Opened in 1995, it is one of the largest water parks in the country. Spanning 8 hectares, it offers numerous water slides, wave pools, lazy river, and children's pools. The park has a capacity of several thousand visitors per day. There are sunbathing lawns and food stalls. Meymadion operates seasonally from June to September. The park uses a water recycling system to reduce environmental impact.",
